---
import ProductLayout from '../../layouts/ProductLayout.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/?$/, '/');
---

<ProductLayout
  title="Tsumly"
  description="Tsumly — a local-first personal expense and loan ledger."
  productName="Tsumly"
  productBase={`${base}products/tsumly/`}
>
  <section>
    <div class="container">
      <h1>Every amount adds up.</h1>
      <p class="muted" style="max-width: 560px;">
        Tsumly is a local-first personal expense and loan ledger. Your money
        stays on your device — no account, no cloud by default — with an
        optional encrypted Google Drive backup when you want one.
      </p>
      <!-- TODO: wire the download link when the release is public -->
      <p>
        <button class="btn btn-primary" type="button" disabled>Download — coming soon</button>
      </p>
      <div class="product-grid">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Smart multi-loan repayment split</h3>
          <p>One repayment, split across several active loans in a single action. Tsumly pre-selects the loans it applies to, shows which will be fully paid and which partially, and never merges loans — a Rs. 3,000 loan repaid by Rs. 1,170 stays one loan with Rs. 1,830 left. A repayment recorded by mistake can be reversed in one step.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Loans that fit real life</h3>
          <p>Lend or borrow, record partial repayments, and mark loans that started before the app — pre-app loans are recorded without moving your current balance. Every loan keeps its own due amount, fees, and history.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>People, not just numbers</h3>
          <p>Loans live on person profiles, so you always see who owes what. A person with an outstanding loan can't be archived by accident, and archived people can still be picked — and are restored automatically.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Private by design</h3>
          <p>Offline-first and one-device-first. Nothing leaves the phone unless you turn on Drive backup, which is encrypted (AES-256-GCM) and stored in the app's own private Drive folder.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
      <p class="muted">In daily use. Privacy and Terms are already live on this site — see the links above.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</ProductLayout>
